{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-15T01:50:26.156Z","author":"claude-hub","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"0400d60929071b1beaa422c1","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.300","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/9","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-15T01:50:26.156Z","author":"claude-hub","text":"Windows CI fix by the orchestrator (2026-10-15). On windows-latest three close differential tests failed. The suggested_retry in close_validation_missing_fields spelled the tracker as the canonical verbatim path (the \\\\?\\ prefix plus the long user directory name), while the Node oracle prints the path as the process sees it (path.resolve, keeping the 8.3 short name). close_item now takes the workspace's query_pm_root (the Node-style lexical path on Windows; identical to the canonical root on Linux) and uses it only for the recovery hint; all filesystem work still uses the canonical root. Unit test close_recovery_spells_the_display_root_not_the_canonical_root fails when the hint uses the canonical root (revert proof). The same commit restores the platform-independent assert_cmd import that the earlier reordering had gated to Linux. just release-check passes locally: tests, 100 percent lines, regions, functions and branches, clippy with deny warnings (also for the x86_64-pc-windows-gnu target), audit, identity and changelog."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-15T01:50:26.156Z"}],"before_hash":"c993df05e86adcf5aa915c7180ef8b65285198197cd51cb027162c5575fa7ca9","after_hash":"6623dd2aaa0c54a2f79fe73ccd3fafc87d9c5fd9ee6c156ba7d680109cb5161e","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file"